# What the Aurora deploy ships.
#
# scripts/aurora-adminbot-host.sh deploys with `git archive`, and that tarball is scp'd over the VPN
# and unpacked into a CS department home directory -- a networked filesystem, where the cost is per
# file rather than per byte. The service runs no tests, so every test file in that archive is paid
# for three times (tar, transfer, extract) and used zero times: 4,207 files and 51 MB of a 119 MB
# archive, a little over a third of the entries.
#
# `export-ignore` affects `git archive` only. Nothing else uses it -- Vercel clones rather than
# archives, and there are no CI workflows -- so this changes the deploy payload and nothing else.
#
# Two directions this can go wrong, both worth knowing before adding a rule here:
#   - A file needed at runtime that only ever appears in the archive is invisible until a release
#     dies on it (see src/agents/workspace/workspace-templates.packaged.test.ts for the last time
#     that happened). Verify a rule by building from an extracted archive, not by reading it.
#   - These patterns match at every level, not just the root. Every directory they currently hit
#     was checked to hold tests and test helpers only.
*.test.ts export-ignore
*.test.tsx export-ignore
*.test.mts export-ignore
*.test.js export-ignore
*.test.mjs export-ignore
*.spec.ts export-ignore
*.test.json export-ignore
test/ export-ignore
__tests__/ export-ignore
